%% Title: A fill that races a cancel, from the router to the risk engine (DR-RV-R03, DR-V12-D13, DR-V12-E09)
sequenceDiagram
  participant S as SmartOrderRouter
  participant B as ChildOrderBook
  participant V as Venue
  participant D as DeskGroup
  participant R as RiskEngine

  S->>B: requestCancel, CancelRequested, prior state kept
  S->>V: OrderCancel (41), wait cancelNanos (2 s)
  alt the fill is reported before the cancel is answered
    V->>D: ExecutionReport fill
    D->>B: booked once by venue and execId
    D->>R: position, through the hedger
    V->>D: ExecutionReport Cancelled for the rest
    D->>S: freed quantity may be routed again
  else the order had already filled, the cancel is refused
    V->>D: ExecutionReport Filled
    V->>D: OrderCancelReject (45)
    Note over V,D: simulator v2 back-test, the same: cancelOrder returns false (DR-V12-E09)
    D->>S: onCancelReject
    S->>B: prior state, if still CancelRequested
    Note over S,B: then one more cancelNanos wait, then cancel again or flag unresolved
  else Cancelled carries a cumQuantity above the fills reported
    V->>D: ExecutionReport Cancelled
    D->>B: frees ordered minus the larger of cum and venueCum
    Note over B: slot kept, waits for the missing fills
    V->>D: late fill
    D->>B: booked, leaves reaches zero, slot released
  else the child was already released
    V->>D: ExecutionReport fill, child unknown to the router
    D->>D: unroutedReports and lateFills counted
    D->>R: onFill once by venue and execId (DR-V12-D13)
    Note over D,R: parent not reopened, hedger sees it in the next residual, a TradeBust reverses it
  end
